    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This now should (finally!) be resolved on latest `main`. Unfortunately, the only approach at fixing this was indeed a new separate option or even two:\n- [`config.options.n_lines`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/ecde5ffd9adfd590d5c2d5d35a7f0152def894fc/doc/mini-indentscope.txt#L165-L166) now limits the number of lines used during scope computation. If computation crosses that threshold (in any direction), scope body's computation is marked [as incomplete](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/ecde5ffd9adfd590d5c2d5d35a7f0152def894fc/doc/mini-indentscope.txt#L293-L294).\n- [`config.draw.predicate`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/ecde5ffd9adfd590d5c2d5d35a7f0152def894fc/doc/mini-indentscope.txt#L136-L138) can be used to decide whether to autodraw scope or not. By default it will not draw scope which computation was incomplete (i.e. scope is too big).\n\nOn huge scopes performance should be good with default `require('mini.indentscope').setup()` with the caveat that the big scopes are not drawn. Tweak that with mentioned config entries.",
            "created_at": "2025-01-16T13:58:04Z",
